  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "&c.-To be brief, in short. वटविटपः &c-it is difficult to see the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "propriety of calling the Vata tree ‘a dayita’; probably the poet",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "refers by dayita’ to गृहस्थाश्रम in which the wife plays a con-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "spicuous part. Let the Vata tree be my home i. e. let me",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "renounce the pleasures of the world and take to a devotee’s life",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "worshipping Si'va sitting under a Vata tree &c.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 6. त्रुटित &c.—the worldly ties which proved an obstruc-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "tion to them having been snapped. आशीविष—a serpent; fr.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "आशी ( a serpent’s fang ) + विष. The derivation more usually",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "given is fr. आशीस् + विष the comp. being classed under the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "पृषोदरादि class. The 2nd l. means ( those blessed persons ) that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "do not seek the crooked course of serpentine sensualism. Mr.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "Telang takes विषम with आशीविष and says ‘the course of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "wordly objects which are like dangerous snakes.’ शरच्चन्द्र &c,—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "the night which is delightful on account of the sky being lit",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "up with the winter moonshine. आभोग—expanse. ( ज्योतिरस्त्यस्याः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "ज्योत्स्ना ). चय storing up. शरण—from शॄ 9 con. to tear.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 7. A question to an estranged friend. Once our in-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "terests were identical; now you and we have no connection.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "What has happened in the meanwhile to estrange us ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 8. अमलपटं—of clean texture. पट्टवस्त्रम्—silken cloth.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "कदशनम्—By Pán. VI. 3. 101. ( see com. ) कत् is substituted for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "कु in a Tat. when the latter member begins with a vowel; coarse",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "food. व्यक्त &c.—The idea is—A man who has renounced the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "world and devoted himself to the service of God entirely is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "indifferent to all such things as are mentioned in the s'loka.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 9. स्मर &c.—Love is often described as blinding men’s",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "eyes, पटुतर &c.—विवेक is here called collyrium because it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "sharpens, restores, or preserves the sight of the mind. समी-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "भूता—Made even, rectified, corrected. Ràmarshi explains it by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "निर्विकल्पा. Mr. Telang takes it to mean ‘looking on all things",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "alike.’",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 10. मान haughtiness. विविक्तम्—lonely, solitary; p. p. of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "विज् with वि. यमिनाम्—of those who restrain their minds ).",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
